# Build output must never enter the image.
#
# The Dockerfile restores inside the container and then publishes with
# --no-restore. Without this file, `COPY src/ src/` drops the host's obj/
# directories on top of that restore, and their project.assets.json points at
# C:\Users\...\.nuget\packages - paths that do not exist in a Linux container.
# publish then fails with NETSDK1064 on packages it cannot find.
#
# The nastier version of the bug is when it *works*: if the host happens to
# have a compatible restore, the image builds from the host's state rather
# than its own, and the build is no longer reproducible.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Not part of the API image. The Dockerfile copies only src/, nuget.config and
# the two Directory.*.props files, so these just bloat the build context.
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vs/
tests/
tools/
eval/
docs/

# Secrets never belong in an image layer, even an intermediate one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
